{%- comment -%}
  `data.filters` is the whole vocabulary — the platform's filters and Liquid's own, serialized into
  one array by the YARD generator in the application repository — so there is nothing to concatenate
  here and no name can appear twice.

  OUTPUT, not `return`: the page renders this partial with `{% render %}`, which discards a returned
  value. Written as a `return` it publishes an empty array, and `filters.json` is how a consumer
  decides whether a filter exists.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function filters = 'api/liquid/platformos_filters', data: data
%}
{{ filters | array_sort_by: 'name' }}
